-- BEFORE <date> is accepted on the act only. On a join line it is refused
-- by name (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.2, built 2026-09-16: the barrier
-- does not lower a DATE there); WITHIN 0 OF <date> is the join line's way to
-- say an absolute date.
IMPORT daydate

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Tenant HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Sign HAS signer IS AN Actor

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
bad MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t MUST Sign (EXACTLY t)
      ONCE ALL HAVE BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 30)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH
